      "refersTo": "composer",
      "description": "One compact writing field and send action.",
      "html": "<form class=\"ds-composer\"><textarea aria-label=\"Message Aksara\" placeholder=\"Message Aksara\u2026\" rows=\"1\"></textarea><button aria-label=\"Send message\" type=\"submit\"><svg width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path d=\"M12 19V5m-7 7 7-7 7 7\"/></svg></button></form>",
      "css": ".ds-composer{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;min-height:48px;padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid var(--line,#e1ddd7);border-radius:11px;background:var(--panel,#fff);color:var(--ink,#242329);font-family:\"Inter Variable\",Inter,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;}.ds-composer textarea{flex:1;min-width:0;min-height:26px;resize:none;padding:4px 5px;border:0;background:transparent;color:var(--ink,#242329);font-size:.875rem;line-height:1.5;font-family:\"Inter Variable\",Inter,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;}.ds-composer textarea:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--green,#75529a);outline-offset:3px;}.ds-composer button{display:grid;place-items:center;width:34px;height:34px;border:0;border-radius:8px;background:var(--green,#75529a);color:var(--primary-foreground,#fff);cursor:pointer;}.ds-composer button:hover{filter:brightness(.97);}.ds-composer button:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--green,#75529a);outline-offset:3px;}.ds-composer button:active{scale:.985;}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Working Reading Room",
    "overview": "Aksara is a working reading room: warm paper, quiet ink, a clear conversation and a document that carries the emphasis. The retained open-triangle mark anchors a compact, labeled interface. The tone is concise and welcoming, with space given to reading and writing rather than atmospheric decoration.\n\nFlat planes and hairline boundaries organize the work. Light mode pairs warm paper with lilac; dark mode changes character to graphite and muted copper. Inter keeps navigation and controls clear, while Georgia gives document paragraphs an editorial reading texture.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Paper and ink planes with restrained tonal separation.",
      "Compact Inter controls and Georgia document paragraphs.",
      "A conversation and its document share one room.",
      "Responsive writing space with explicit context and save state."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Reading Accent Rule",
        "body": "Use lilac on warm paper and copper on graphite for primary actions, selected navigation and interaction emphasis. The legacy CSS name \u201cgreen\u201d denotes this accent role, not a green hue.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Voices Rule",
        "body": "Keep interface text, document titles and headings in Inter. Use Georgia for document paragraphs; do not apply the serif indiscriminately to controls, lists or the whole editor.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Room Rule",
        "body": "Keep working planes flat at rest. Reserve soft shadows for temporary overlays and the phone launcher dock.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do keep audience, save state and source context readable beside the actual work.",
      "Do preserve a direct named conversation return when the adjacent thread is hidden.",
      "Do use the implemented accent outline for keyboard focus and respect reduced motion.",
      "Do give phone inputs a readable 1rem size and account for the bottom safe area."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't introduce atmospheric wallpaper or decorative blobs into the Reading Room.",
      "Don't turn every work item into a floating dashboard card; use hairline-separated rows where the implementation does.",
      "Don't substitute blue-slate dark surfaces for the graphite and copper palette.",
      "Don't imply live collaboration, real contributors or real model activity through decorative presence or fabricated content."
    ]
  }
